up and down for you.

01:18:01.970 --> 01:18:03.720
Now, this scaling both directions

01:18:03.720 --> 01:18:06.790
is referred to as, elasticity.

01:18:06.790 --> 01:18:09.410
Function-as-a-Service, or FaaS,

01:18:09.410 --> 01:18:12.590
is the idea at the core of serverless.

01:18:12.590 --> 01:18:14.040
Basically, you write a function,

01:18:14.040 --> 01:18:16.900
and you follow the specific parameters.

01:18:16.900 --> 01:18:18.360
The provider handles all

01:18:18.360 --> 01:18:20.730
the routing responses and scaling.

01:18:20.730 --> 01:18:22.350
All of the big cloud players

01:18:22.350 --> 01:18:24.360
have some sort of version of this,

01:18:24.360 --> 01:18:26.780
and typically the executions are free,

01:18:26.780 --> 01:18:28.720
until you hit a certain threshold.

01:18:28.720 --> 01:18:32.220
Even then, you only pay for
when the function executes.

01:18:32.220 --> 01:18:35.340
This can lead to tremendous cost savings,

01:18:35.340 --> 01:18:38.580
also because there's
only ever one function,

01:18:38.580 --> 01:18:42.131
